-- title:
--   Finite generation of the relation module over ℤ
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite group and let $B$ be a representation of $G$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose underlying type is finite. Write $\mathrm{Rep.free}\ \mathbb{Z}\ G\ B$ for the free $\mathbb{Z}[G]$-representation generated by the underlying set of $B$ and `freeCover B` for the canonical equivariant map from it onto $B$; then [`Rep.relationModule B`](def/GroupCohomology_RelationModule.html#L18) is the subrepresentation of $\mathrm{Rep.free}\ \mathbb{Z}\ G\ B$ cut out by the kernel of the underlying linear map of `freeCover B`, a submodule which is $G$-stable because `freeCover B` is equivariant, and [`Rep.relationCarrier B`](def/GroupCohomology_RelationModule.html#L50) is the type whose definition unfolds to this representation, equipped with its $\mathbb{Z}$-module structure. The assertion is that [`Rep.relationCarrier B`](def/GroupCohomology_RelationModule.html#L50) is a finite $\mathbb{Z}$-module in the sense of `Module.Finite`, i.e. it is generated by finitely many elements as an abelian group. No hypothesis beyond the finiteness of $G$ and of the underlying type of $B$ is imposed.
--
--   This records that the relation module $R(B)=\ker(\mathbb{Z}[G]^{(B)}\to B)$ attached to a finite representation of a finite group is a finitely generated abelian group (hence free of finite rank, being torsion-free). It is used in the cohomological bookkeeping around [`Rep.relationModule`](def/GroupCohomology_RelationModule.html#L18), notably by [`Rep.finite_H1_ihom_relationModuleInt`](thm.html#Rep.finite_H1_ihom_relationModuleInt), [`Rep.exists_hom_relationModuleInt_forall_map_delta_eq`](thm.html#Rep.exists_hom_relationModuleInt_forall_map_delta_eq) and [`Rep.forall_map_delta_eq_zero_iff_exists_eq_sum_rho`](thm.html#Rep.forall_map_delta_eq_zero_iff_exists_eq_sum_rho).
